From adca5ca2f4a3238624fefa9411968dcb71ae062c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] winedmo: stream progressive HTTP VOD through FFmpeg

Ordinary HTTP(S) media currently enters WineDMO only after URLMon finishes a
cached download. Prefer FFmpeg's direct network I/O so a finite VOD can begin
while later bytes are still arriving.

Keep GE's explicit HLS route ahead of generic HTTP and classify HLS markers
only in the URL path, before query or fragment data. Apply cooperative
interrupt deadlines to direct HTTP open, read, seek, stream-info, and close
calls. Require a range-seekable AVIO context before advertising seek support
for generic HTTP without changing HLS/RTSP seekability.

Restrict generic nested protocols to HTTP(S), an explicitly configured HTTP
proxy, TCP, and TLS. HLS adds only FFmpeg's crypto wrapper for AES-128 segments;
the nested segment remains constrained by the root-sensitive HTTP(S) list. A
plain HTTP root may upgrade to HTTPS, but an HTTPS root cannot downgrade to
plaintext. Force TLS certificate and hostname verification for progressive
HTTP and the initial HLS playlist. Preserve progressive HTTP trust options
across redirects and range reopens. HLS child requests require the project's
companion FFmpeg TLS-default hardening. AES-128 HLS also requires the companion
GE build-enable patch because the pinned build disables CONFIG_CRYPTO_PROTOCOL.

Return a distinguished, narrowly checked NTSTATUS only when a plain HTTP
direct open returns AVERROR_INVALIDDATA without timeout or cancellation. In
the pinned FFmpeg, certificate and hostname failures return AVERROR(EIO), while
protocol-whitelist and downgrade rejections return AVERROR(EINVAL); both stay
terminal. Never send an HTTPS input to URLMon. The Windows scheme handler uses
the narrow signal to attempt the old cached-byte-stream path once. Interrupted
opens, later demux or media-source failures do not trigger a second transfer,
and classified HLS never falls back.

Never pass FFmpeg's network AVIO state to Wine's custom-stream MP4 metadata,
duration-scan, or raw-MPEG seek helpers. Add privacy-safe route markers without
interpolating the URL. This experimental Alpha patch still requires direct
HTTP, non-range, fallback, cancellation, source replacement, and VRChat
lobby-sync tests before release. URLMon fallback is still full-cache and has
no project timeout. Page URL resolution, including yt-dlp, is intentionally
out of scope.

The license of the modified Wine source files applies to this patch.

A3.19: rebased after GE-Proton11-6's ge-video-rework set.
The generic direct HTTP route also covers signed Googlevideo streams. Replace GE's separate reconnecting shortcut with that bounded, TLS-verified route; keep no automatic reconnect and manual reopen semantics.
A3.21: identify HTTP(S) media requests as Windows Media Foundation, matching
Proton-RTSP's working media client. FFmpeg carries this user_agent option
through redirects, range reopens, and HLS child requests. This changes no
TLS, protocol, fallback, timeout, or retry policy. The local compatibility
case is separate from confirming the reported service in VRChat.
A3.22: do not infer HTTP HLS segment content from its filename extension.
The captured service uses MPEG-TS behind web-looking suffixes; A3.21 rejects
its playlist before reading those segments. Restrict detected HLS formats
instead, including child demuxers, while retaining TLS and protocol limits.
This is not a retry or a service-domain special case.
